    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d842-a3">

                <pb facs="0839" n="673" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg673"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3—Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Government for the Danish West Indian
                        Islands</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 76a</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">St. Thomas</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-03-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 22, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Government begs to report that it, on application from Ejnar Svendsen, civil
                    engineer, of Roskilde, for permission to establish and carry on an electric
                    plant to supply the town with electric light, has granted Mr. Svendsen the said
                    permission. The committee for buildings and streets had previously sanctioned
                    his application.</p>
                <p>Please find enclosed a copy of Mr. Svendsen’s application and his license.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>
                                <hi rendition="#small-caps">Helweg Larsen</hi>
                            </item>
                            <item>
                                <hi rendition="#small-caps">Will Jacobsen</hi>
                            </item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
